ng.call/reason :missing-raise-exit}))))))\\\\n  1402\\\\t                       u/capture)\\\\n  1403\\\\t          routed (if (::invoker env)\\\\n  1404\\\\t                   (u/if-node\\\\n  1405\\\\t                     (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'data/map?) (u/v callee))\\\\n  1406\\\\t                                (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'data/contains?) (u/v callee) (u/lit :yang.call/entry))\\\\n  1407\\\\t                                           (u/lit true)\\\\n  1408\\\\t                                           (cell-ref-shaped-node (u/v callee)))\\\\n  1409\\\\t                                (u/lit false))\\\\n  1410\\\\t                     admitted\\\\n  2410\\\\t;; Guest-side source, compiled through this compiler like any program: the\\\\n  2411\\\\t;; functions that invoke guest closures (map, filter, reduce, comp, partial)\\\\n  2412\\\\t;; must run on the VM, never on the host, because a closure is a VM value. It\\\\n  2413\\\\t;; is written for the argument-vector convention with the outcome model, so a\\\\n  2414\\\\t;; closure it calls is unwrapped by the compiler's own early-return pattern\\\\n  2415\\\\t;; and a closure's failure ends the library function with the same outcome.\\\\n  2416\\\\t;;\\\\n  2417\\\\t;; What is derived, from the VM primitives and the `data` module only:\\\\n  2418\\\\t;; identity, inc/dec, second, the collection predicates (coll?/vector?/map?/\\\\n  2419\\\\t;; set?/seq?/list?/sequential?, from the `portable/*` adapters of data/count,\\\\n  2420\\\\t;; peek, dissoc and disj: a refusal as data says \\\\\\\"not that kind\\\\\\\"), boolean?,\\\\n  2421\\\\t;; fn? (data/callable?), seq, rem, reverse, list, cons, vector, count,\\\\n  2422\\\\t;; contains?, rest, map/mapv/filter/remove/reduce (with reduced)/into/concat/merge,\\\\n  2423\\\\t;; keys/vals/disj and set union/difference,\\\\n  2424\\\\t;; comp, partial, gensym (explicit supply), not=, and `apply`, which is a\\\\n  2425\\\\t;; compiler intrinsic over the convention's argument vector.\\\\n  2426\\\\t;;\\\\n  2427\\\\t;; What stays a host primitive, named by the `kind` module: a symbol, a\\\\n  2428\\\\t;; keyword and a host string are distinguished or built only by the host\\\\n  2429\\\\t;; (symbol?, keyword?, name, symbol, keyword, str, int?), as is metadata access\\\\n  2430\\\\t;; (meta and with-meta). The current data ABI has no metadata-write export,\\\\n  2431\\\\t;; so with-meta is an explicit pure representation seam, not an ambient store.\\\\n  2432\\\\t;; No VM primitive tells a symbol from a keyword. Clojure Var identity is an\\\\n  2433\\\\t;; explicitly admitted kind/var? seam on the JVM; namespace lookup (resolve)\\\\n  2434\\\\t;; still requires a separately installed host capability.\\\\n  2435\\\\t;;\\\\n  2436\\\\t;; Known compromises: `reduced` is an untyped tagged map, so reduced? matches\\\\n  2437\\\\t;; any map holding :yin.k/reduced true; seq refuses a non-collection (a string\\\\n  2438\\\\t;; is the data module's str-* ops, not a seq); eager sequences are lists;\\\\n  2439\\\\t;; rem rejects non-integers and a zero divisor before arithmetic; the compiler\\\\n  2440\\\\t;; emits bare conj and vec, so a program may not define or bind either.\\\\n  2441\\\\t;; When collection calls are needed, invoke-value is a library helper whose\\\\n  2442\\\\t;; local capture is refused explicitly.\\\\n  2443\\\\t;;\\\\n  2444\\\\t;; Variadic Clojure functions are fixed-arity here (the convention has no\\\\n  2445\\\\t;; variadic parameter): str, list and vector admit 0 to 6 arguments, concat and\\\\n  2446\\\\t;; merge 0 to 4, union 0 to 6, difference 2, comp 0 to 3, partial binds 1 to 3.\\\\n  2447\\\\t;; A larger count is the\\\\n  2448\\\\t;; function's own arity error.\\\\n  2449\\\\t\\\\n  2450\\\\t(def library-adapters\\\\n  2451\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The `:adapters` a program using `library` is compiled with: the data\\\\n  2452\\\\t   exports whose refusal the predicates read as data. The harness registers\\\\n  2453\\\\t   `portable/<name>` as `outcome-adapter` over the same `data/<name>`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  2454\\\\t  {'data/count 'portable/count\\\\n  2455\\\\t   'data/peek 'portable/peek\\\\n  2456\\\\t   'data/dissoc 'portable/dissoc\\\\n  2457\\\\t   'data/disj 'portable/disj\\\\n  2458\\\\t   'data/str-length 'portable/str-length})\\\\n  2459\\\\t\\\\n  2460\\\\t\\\\n  2461\\\\t(def kind-module\\\\n  2462\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The `kind` host module's exports, symbol to host function: the irreducible\\\\n  2463\\\\t   kind and name primitives (see the library notes). Every export is pure.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  2464\\\\t  (merge\\\\n  2465\\\\t    {'symbol? symbol?\\\\n  2466\\\\t     'keyword? keyword?\\\\n  2467\\\\t     'name name\\\\n  2468\\\\t     'symbol symbol\\\\n  2469\\\\t     'keyword keyword\\\\n  2470\\\\t     'str str\\\\n  2471\\\\t     'int? int?\\\\n  2472\\\\t     'with-meta with-meta\\\\n  2473\\\\t     'meta meta}\\\\n  2474\\\\t    #?(:clj {'var? var?} :default {})))\\\\n  2475\\\\t\\\\n  2476\\\\t\\\\n  2477\\\\t(def kind-arities\\\\n  2478\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The published arities of each `kind` export.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  2479\\\\t  {'symbol? [1], 'keyword? [1], 'name [1], 'symbol [1 2], 'keyword [1 2]\\\\n  2480\\\\t   'str [0 1 2 3 4 5 6 :variadic], 'int? [1], 'var? [1], 'with-meta [2], 'meta [1]})\\\\n  2481\\\\t\\\\n  2482\\\\t\\\\n  2483\\\\t(def library\\\\n  2484\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The library's definitions, in order, as quoted source.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  2485\\\\t  '[(defn identity\\\\n  2486\\\\t      [x]\\\\n  2487\\\\t      x)\\\\n  2488\\\\t    (defn inc\\\\n  2489\\\\t      [x]\\\\n  2490\\\\t      (+ x 1))\\\\n  2491\\\\t    (defn dec\\\\n  2492\\\\t      [x]\\\\n  2493\\\\t      (- x 1))\\\\n  2494\\\\t    (defn second\\\\n  2495\\\\t      [x]\\\\n  2496\\\\t      (first (rest x)))\\\\n  2497\\\\t    (defn not=\\\\n  2498\\\\t      [a b]\\\\n  2499\\\\t      (not (= a b)))\\\\n  2500\\\\t    (defn boolean?\\\\n  2501\\\\t      [x]\\\\n  2502\\\\t      (or (= x true) (