aped-node\\\\n  1246\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The UAST test that the callee node could be a cell reference the\\\\n  1247\\\\t   VM issued: `:type :cell-ref` with the `:id` and `:seal` every\\\\n  1248\\\\t   issued reference carries, no other entries, a seal of the issued\\\\n  1249\\\\t   form (a 64-character string), and an `:id` in the engine's heap\\\\n  1250\\\\t   id language — every cell id is a `:cell-N` keyword (engine\\\\n  1251\\\\t   `gen-id` mints them all from one counter), so an `:id` that is\\\\n  1252\\\\t   not such a keyword names no cell the task could ever have\\\\n  1253\\\\t   minted and the map is data, whatever its other entries spell.\\\\n  1254\\\\t   A map that fails this test is never dereferenced: it routes to\\\\n  1255\\\\t   ordinary map invocation, which grants no cell capability. A map\\\\n  1256\\\\t   that passes it is a dereference *candidate*, not a proven\\\\n  1257\\\\t   reference — authenticity is the VM's heap+seal check at the\\\\n  1258\\\\t   dereference, which this frontend cannot observe (a failed\\\\n  1259\\\\t   check is a host-level refusal, outside every guest catch), so\\\\n  1260\\\\t   the candidate is offered to admission and the VM governs:\\\\n  1261\\\\t   genuine references dereference to their cell's entry, and a\\\\n  1262\\\\t   forged candidate fails closed in the VM exactly as any forged\\\\n  1263\\\\t   reference must.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  1264\\\\t  [callee]\\\\n  1265\\\\t  (let [seal (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) callee (u/lit :seal))\\\\n  1266\\\\t        id (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) callee (u/lit :id))\\\\n  1267\\\\t        id-names-cell?\\\\n  1268\\\\t        (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'kind/keyword?) id)\\\\n  1269\\\\t                   (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\\\\n  1270\\\\t                                     (u/app (u/v 'data/str-index-of)\\\\n  1271\\\\t                                            (u/app (u/v 'kind/name) id)\\\\n  1272\\\\t                                            (u/lit \\\\\\\"cell-